# Feature: heap-free scalar `Display` renderers. `print(int)` formats digits into a
# fixed STACK buffer (div/mod-by-10, no allocator) then writes them — covering zero, a
# negative value (leading `-`), and a multi-digit value. `print(bool)` inlines a branch over
# the `true`/`false` cstrings. The `"\n"` separators exercise the unchanged `print(str)` path.
fn main() {
    print(0)
    print("\n")
    print(-13)
    print("\n")
    print(4200)
    print("\n")
    print(true)
    print("\n")
    print(false)
}
# expect: stdout "0\n-13\n4200\ntrue\nfalse"
# expect: exit 0
